      "text": [
        "966 - وَقَالَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: «اَلْجُلُوسُ بَعْدَ صَلاَةِ اَلْغَدَاةِ فِي اَلتَّعْقِيبِ وَ اَلدُّعَاءِ حَتَّى تَطْلُعَ اَلشَّمْسُ أَبْلَغُ فِي طَلَبِ اَلرِّزْقِ مِنَ اَلضَّرْبِ فِي اَلْأَرْضِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.966 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) said:\n\"Sitting after the dawn (Fajr) prayer in contemplation (ta'qeeb) and supplication until the sun rises is more effective in seeking sustenance than striving to earn it through labor on the earth”."
        ]
      }
